    "encrypted": "false",
    "title": "Final Project: Responsible AI Use Guide",
    "long_instructions": "#### Students' work throughout the unit will drive toward a **Responsible AI Use Guide** that synthesizes their learnings about how best to work with (and without!) AI in multiple domains. \r\n\r\n#### The following description is provided for students in the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wzOsVT4b0Lt0y4GH9AmKuSd6ceWOoN_0Uq1wYFb6V3g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Unit Project Guide</a>:\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 15px; margin: 20px 0px;\">\r\n\r\n  <!-- Icon -->\r\n  <img src=\"https://images.code.org/3f2b3d032f7e00c6710aaac790be927f-image-1772831348884.png\"\r\n       alt=\"\"\r\n       style=\"width: 80px; height: auto; flex-shrink: 0;\">\r\n\r\n  <!-- Callout Box -->\r\n  <div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 100%;\">\r\n\r\n#### In this unit, you will test AI, look for patterns, identify risks, and decide how it should be used responsibly in real situations.\r\n\r\n#### You will design your guide in a style and theme inspired by the rulebooks, playbooks, and explainer formats you already recognize and trust.\r\n\r\n#### By the end, you will create a clear, student-friendly **Responsible AI Use Guide** that includes visual systems, boundaries, and credibility checks. This is a set of guidance, created by you, backed by your testing.\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\n#### **Your guide will help others answer questions like**:\r\n\r\n- #### When is AI helpful?\r\n- #### When should we slow down and double-check?\r\n- #### How much information is too much to share?\r\n- #### When does AI stop helping and start replacing human thinking?\r\n- #### How do we stay in control?\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<!-- Public Product Generation -->\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; margin: 20px 0; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;\">\r\n  <img src=\"https://images.code.org/234056f4fd813d75217d121475d904b7-image-1772670604478.png\"\r\n       alt=\"\" style=\"width: 40px; height: 40px;\">\r\n  <div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;\">PBL Design Element: Public Product Generation</p>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-style: italic; margin: 5px 0 0 0; line-height: 1.3;\">\r\n      Each project culminates in a tangible product shared beyond the individual student to reinforce purpose and accountability.\r\n    </p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n## Example Guides\r\n\r\n#### 📎 <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1Hb6D3ohPC7uicvVNO7V7fvLVeQXx_4aJplO5HYrHuR8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Resource: Example Guides</a>\r\n\r\n#### Look through the example guides in the resource above. Students will peruse similar guides as inspiration for their own **Responsible AI Use Guides**. While you browse the slide deck, consider the following:\r\n\r\n* #### What will pique my students' interest from the sample guides?\r\n* #### What will my students excel at in creating their own guides? What will I need to do to support their development of a guide?\r\n\r\n#### Jot your answers in the open response box below.\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\n##### **Note:** Click and drag the bottom-right corner of the reflection box below to expand it.",
